# Button Cursor

Apply to every clickable **button** in the web UI (`<button>`, including icon-only and submit buttons).

## Rules

1. **Pointer cursor** — Buttons must show `cursor: pointer`. Global styles in `src/app/globals.css` set this on all `button` elements.

2. **Disabled state** — Disabled buttons use `cursor: not-allowed` (also set globally on `button:disabled`).

3. **Do not override** — Do not add `cursor-default` (or other non-pointer cursors) to buttons. Table cells and other non-button wrappers may keep `cursor-default` when they only stop event propagation.

4. **Shared button components** — Prefer shared controls under `components/shared/` (`action-icon-buttons`, `back-button`, etc.) so cursor behavior stays consistent.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — overrides pointer on a button
<button className="cursor-default ...">Edit</button>

// ✅ GOOD — rely on global button cursor (optional explicit class is fine)
<button type="button" className="rounded-md border ...">Edit</button>
```
